extern def $IntrinsicObjects { sig "IntrinsicObjects(): a List of Records" meaning "The objects of <emu-xref href=\"#sec-createintrinsics\"></emu-xref> step 2, one new Record each, in an order in which each comes after the objects its [[Prototype]] names: the well-known intrinsic objects of <emu-xref href=\"#table-well-known-intrinsic-objects\"></emu-xref> and every object their properties hold, as clauses <emu-xref href=\"#sec-global-object\"></emu-xref> through <emu-xref href=\"#sec-reflection\"></emu-xref>, <emu-xref href=\"#sec-additional-built-in-properties\"></emu-xref>, <emu-xref href=\"#sec-%throwtypeerror%\"></emu-xref> and <emu-xref href=\"#sec-%foriniteratorprototype%-object\"></emu-xref> specify them. Each Record has the fields [[Index]] (its position in the List), [[Names]] (a List of the [[Intrinsics]] field names it is recorded under: its intrinsic names, with and without the enclosing %), [[Prototype]] (the position of its [[Prototype]], or *null*), [[Exotic]] (the clause defining its kind of exotic object, or ~empty~), [[Extensible]], [[Slots]] (a List of its specified internal slots' names), [[SlotValues]] (a List of Records with fields [[Name]] and [[Value]], the specified values of those slots), and [[Properties]] (a List of its properties' Records, as ClauseProperties gives them, in document order, with [[Object]], [[Get]] and [[Set]] the positions of objects in the List). A built-in function object's Record also has [[Behaviour]] (its algorithm steps, or the clause that gives its behaviour), [[Length]], [[Name]] (its *\"name\"* property's key), [[Prefix]] (*\"get\"*, *\"set\"*, or ~empty~), [[Constructor]], [[Async]] (whether it is described as async), [[LengthAttributes]] and [[NameAttributes]] (Records with fields [[Writable]], [[Enumerable]] and [[Configurable]]); for any other object [[Behaviour]] is ~empty~." }
